    "ogHeadline": "SUMMER\nMADNESS 15",
    "ogAccent": "8A1E2E",
    "heroCredit": "VerseTracker",
    "heroCreditUrl": "https://versetracker.com/media",
    "body": "## TL;DR\n\nSummer Madness is URL's biggest card of the year, and the fifteenth one is September 21 in London. Loaded Lux vs Nu Jerzey Twork was the first battle announced. The new piece: Geechi Gotti vs Shotty Horroh is on the card now. Eleven days out.\n\n## What's new\n\nWhen we first mentioned this card in August, it was one battle and a date. Now it's a card. Gotti is the addition that changes the temperature — he's the most consistent battler of the last decade, a multiple Champion of the Year, and he doesn't lose rounds to pressure. Shotty Horroh is the UK's best-known name on the American circuit, which makes sense for a London stage.\n\n## Why Lux vs Twork is the headline\n\nLoaded Lux is a legend. \"You gon' get this work\" is a decade old and still gets quoted like scripture. He doesn't battle often, and when he does, it's an event. Nu Jerzey Twork is the opposite kind of battler — all energy, punchlines stacked on top of each other, crowd on its feet. Legend versus momentum. Pen versus performance. That's the fight.\n\n## The bigger picture\n\nSmack White built URL into the biggest Black-owned league in the sport, and he's spent the last few years pushing it back toward big rooms. Taking the flagship to London isn't a retreat from New York — it's a flex. The audience for this is global, and the numbers on YouTube prove it every month.\n\nWe spotlight URL for the same reason we spotlight Black-owned anything: the culture built it, and the culture should own it.\n\n## Before you tape\n\nBattle rap lives on X. Cards change late. Confirm the final matchups on @urltv before you say them on camera.\n\n## Sources\n\n- [VerseTracker — Battle rap media index](https://versetracker.com/media)\n- [Ultimate Rap League on X](https://x.com/urltv)\n- [Ebony — Smack Mitchell on battle rap's rebirth](https://www.ebony.com/ultimate-rap-league-troy-smack-mitchell-battle-rap/)",
    "goLiveAt": "2026-09-22"
