    "title": "Cyberpunk Goes Cardboard: TCG Beta Starts Now",
    "headline": "Night City,\nOn the Table.",
    "subhead": "The Cyberpunk 2077 Trading Card Game runs in-store beta events September 10-17 ahead of a November 6 release, the same week the game leaves Game Pass.",
    "description": "Cyberpunk 2077's TCG beta runs Sept 10-17 before its Nov 6 launch, and the game exits Xbox Game Pass Sept 15. Sneakz & Beatz on the $28M card game.",
    "keywords": [
      "Cyberpunk 2077 TCG",
      "Cyberpunk trading card game",
      "Cyberpunk TCG beta",
      "Cyberpunk 2077 Game Pass",
      "CD Projekt Red",
      "WeirdCo",
      "Sneakz and Beatz",
      "PHRHX"
    ],
    "ogHeadline": "Night City, On the Table.",
    "ogAccent": "F5E400",
    "heroCredit": "CD Projekt Red / WeirdCo",
    "heroCreditUrl": "https://screenrant.com/cyberpunk-2077-tcg-beta-september-2026/",
    "trendScore": 84,
    "body": "Cyberpunk gets a beat every episode. This week it's not a patch and it's not the sequel. It's cards. The official Cyberpunk 2077 Trading Card Game is running its first in-store beta events from September 10 through the 17th, about two months ahead of the full release on November 6, 2026.\n\n## How the beta works\nYou don't need to own a single card. Local game stores that opted in are selling a Beta Event Kit that includes everything for a deck, and the events run as sealed play. The Cyberpunk TCG site has a store locator and a primer for people who've never touched a TCG. It's Night City's version of a prerelease weekend.\n\n## Why the design is different\nDeveloper WeirdCo built it with CD Projekt Red, and it doesn't use a normal life-point system. The engine runs on dice called Gigs. You complete contracts, earn Eddies, steal your opponent's dice mid-combat, and build Street Cred to play the heavy cards. That's the game's economy turned into a mechanic, and it's why it doesn't play like a Magic clone with a Cyberpunk skin.\n\n## The money behind it\nThe Kickstarter pulled more than $28 million from over 50,000 backers, the most-funded TCG in Kickstarter history. Johnny Silverhand's on a card. Jackie's on a card. This isn't a licensing afterthought.\n\n## The other date this week\nCyberpunk 2077 leaves Xbox Game Pass on September 15. If you've been playing V's story on the subscription and never finished Phantom Liberty, that's your deadline. The game's done getting expansions, so what's there is the complete package.\n\nSame universe, three fronts: the TCG on tables in September, Edgerunners 2 on Netflix in October, Cyberpunk 2 still cooking. Night City isn't slowing down.\n\n## Sources\n- Screen Rant - A new Cyberpunk 2077 game is coming this September (TCG beta): https://screenrant.com/cyberpunk-2077-tcg-beta-september-2026/\n- Cyberpunk 2077 Wiki (Fextralife) - Cyberpunk Trading Card Game: https://cyberpunk2077.wiki.fextralife.com/Cyberpunk_Trading_Card_Game\n- CBR - Cyberpunk 2077 leaving Xbox Game Pass September 15: https://www.cbr.com/xbox-game-pass-leaving-september-2026-cyberpunk-2077/",
