    "heroCredit": "Crunchyroll via Final Weapon",
    "heroCreditUrl": "https://finalweapon.net/2026/09/06/crunchyroll-anime-nights-reveals-september-2026-showings/",
    "heroImage": "https://finalweapon.net/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Crunchyroll-Anime-Nights-Reveals-September-2026-Showings.webp",
    "trendScore": 64,
    "body": "Black Clover has been off the air since March 2021. Season 2 finally streams on Crunchyroll October 3, but the first episode hits theaters twelve days earlier. Per [Crunchyroll](https://www.crunchyroll.com/news/announcements/2026/9/1/crunchyroll-anime-nights-september-sneak-peek-tickets-on-sale) (@Crunchyroll) and [Final Weapon](https://finalweapon.net/2026/09/06/crunchyroll-anime-nights-reveals-september-2026-showings/), the September Anime Nights Sneak Peek runs September 21 in US (Fandango) and Canadian (Cineplex) theaters, Japanese audio with English subs.\n\n!youtube(https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=BwdMT-OiARI)\n\n## The bill\nBlack Clover Season 2 is the headliner; the screening also previews The Vermilion Mask, Overgeared, Firefly Wedding (david production, the JoJo studio, streaming October 9) and PSYREN. Five fall premieres, one ticket.\n\n## What Season 2 is\nThe Spade Kingdom Raid arc, the stretch of Yuki Tabata's manga that the 2017-21 anime never reached. Ayataka Tanemura, who directed the original series and the Sword of the Wizard King film, is back in the chair at Studio Pierrot. Wanima does the opening. The second trailer dropped at Anime Expo in July; this is the payoff.\n\n## Why we care\nBlack Clover is the shonen that Black anime fans adopted hardest in the late 2010s: an underdog with no magic in a world built on it, the loudest protagonist on television, and a soundtrack that got remixed on every corner of Black Twitter. Asta's return in a theater full of people who waited five years is going to be a communal moment, which is the whole point of putting an episode on a screen instead of an app. If Dream Con had a sound, it was the Black Clover OP.\n\n## Sources\n- Crunchyroll - Anime Nights September Sneak Peek: Tickets On Sale (Sept. 1, 2026): https://www.crunchyroll.com/news/announcements/2026/9/1/crunchyroll-anime-nights-september-sneak-peek-tickets-on-sale\n- Final Weapon - Crunchyroll Anime Nights Reveals September 2026 Showings (Sept. 6, 2026): https://finalweapon.net/2026/09/06/crunchyroll-anime-nights-reveals-september-2026-showings/\n- Crunchyroll News - Black Clover Season 2 Anime Announces October 2026 Release (June 15, 2026): https://www.crunchyroll.com/news/latest/2026/6/15/black-clover-season-2-anime-october-2026-release-date-director",
