    "ogHeadline": "STEEL DID IT TWICE.",
    "ogAccent": "B8860B",
    "heroCredit": "Alberto E. Rodriguez / Getty Images, courtesy Complex",
    "heroCreditUrl": "https://www.complex.com/music/a/jadegomez510/brian-steel-lil-durk-not-guilty-reactions",
    "heroImage": "https://images.complex.com/complex/image/upload/ar_1.91,c_fill,g_auto,q_auto,w_1200/sanity-new/aojcbkf5mdtejxmt92yv",
    "trendScore": 94,
    "body": "The verdict was the story at 5 p.m. By 8 p.m. the story was the lawyer. When Brian Steel walked out of the federal courthouse in downtown Los Angeles on Friday, September 11, the crowd that had been camped outside for three days of deliberation swarmed him and started chanting MVP, per [Complex](https://www.complex.com/music/a/jadegomez510/brian-steel-lil-durk-not-guilty-reactions) (@complex). Two summers ago it was Young Thug walking out of Fulton County on a plea Steel negotiated after getting himself held in contempt for his client. Now it's [Lil Durk, not guilty on all five counts](/the-lane/lil-durk-not-guilty-all-counts-murder-for-hire-verdict-2026) in a case where prosecutors said he \"had his shooters on speed dial.\" Thug's reaction on X was three words: \"thank me later.\"\n\n## The room and the reaction\n[HotNewHipHop](https://www.hotnewhiphop.com/1009386-lil-durk-verdict-hip-hop-reacts) (@HotNewHipHop) has the roll call. DJ Akademiks was live on stream when the count came back and looked stunned, which is its own kind of poetry, because a clip from his 2023 sit-down with Durk was part of what the government played in closings. G Herbo and Doe Boy posted celebration videos. 21 Savage posted a photo of him and Durk. Ye reposted the news. Meek Mill, who caught heat last week for a \"Free Durk\" post, answered with a string of praying hands. Cordae compared Steel to Johnnie Cochran. 50 Cent went a different direction and gave the flowers to Drew Findling, the other half of Durk's defense, who told cameras during deliberations that \"the voice is innocent.\"\n\nBoosie's post was the one that will get quoted the longest: \"WHEN U DONT RAT U COME BACK.\" That's the code the whole trial was actually about, and the jury heard it argued from both sides for three weeks.\n\n![Lil Durk before a White Sox game in Chicago, May 2022](https://www.hotnewhiphop.com/imgprst/2292x1200-fit-81-auto/2026/09/durk1-scaled-e1789169848680.jpg \"Kamil Krzaczynski / USA TODAY Sports, via HotNewHipHop|https://www.hotnewhiphop.com/1009386-lil-durk-verdict-hip-hop-reacts\")\n\n## What Steel actually did\nThe government's case was built on OTF insiders who flipped: Kacey \"OTF Jam\" Hester, Kavon \"OTF Vonnie\" Grant, Keith \"Flacka\" Jones. Steel's closing didn't try to explain away the texts or the lyrics. He went at the men. He told the jury Hester \"is not human,\" called the cooperators serial killers pointing at a star to save themselves, and floated Vonnie, King Von's own cousin, as the person who actually ran the 2022 plot on Quando Rondo. \"They put a target on a human being. A celebrity human being. That's why you're here.\"\n\nThe split verdict says the jury bought it. Deandre \"OTF DeDe\" Wilson and David \"Browneyez\" Lindsey were convicted on the stalking counts and acquitted on murder-for-hire. So the panel believed a plot existed and that those two were in it. They didn't believe the government proved Durk ordered it or paid for it. That's a surgical result, not a blanket one, and it's the same shape as the YSL outcome: the star walks, the circle doesn't.\n\n## Why he isn't home\nDurk was ordered to stay in custody. The racketeering indictment that was added earlier this year was severed from this trial in July, and Judge Fitzgerald has the RICO case set for October 5, per [Complex](https://www.complex.com/music/a/tracewilliamcowen/lil-durk-conviction-prison-time). That trial is about whether OTF itself was an enterprise, which is a different question with a different evidence pile, and the feds have already said they'll fight release in the meantime. Friday night was a win. It was not the end.\n\n## The cultural close\nEvery big federal rap case of this decade now runs through the same lawyer, and the culture has noticed. Steel's name is a punchline in the good sense: Thug, Durk, and a swarm of fans chanting a sports acronym at a defense attorney on a sidewalk. That's a shift. The old story was the industry watching a rapper go down and posting RIP-style captions after. The new one is a whole ecosystem, from the streamers who covered the trial daily to the artists who posted before the verdict was an hour old, treating a not-guilty like a championship. Whether that survives October 5 is the next question. Steel will be in the room for that one too.\n\n## Sources\n- Complex, September 11-12, 2026 - Lil Durk Fans Swarm Brian Steel in Celebration After Rapper Beats Murder-For-Hire Case: https://www.complex.com/music/a/jadegomez510/brian-steel-lil-durk-not-guilty-reactions\n- Complex, September 11-12, 2026 - Kanye West and More React to Verdict in Lil Durk's Murder-for-Hire Case: https://www.complex.com/music/a/jaelaniturnerwilliams/celebrities-react-lil-durk-verdict\n- HotNewHipHop, September 11, 2026 - Lil Durk Not Guilty: Ye, G Herbo, Meek Mill, Young Thug and More React: https://www.hotnewhiphop.com/1009386-lil-durk-verdict-hip-hop-reacts\n- XXL, September 11, 2026 - Lil Durk Found Not Guilty on All Charges in Murder-for-Hire Trial: https://www.xxlmag.com/lil-durk-not-guilty-murder-for-hire-trial/\n- Complex, September 2026 - Lil Durk Trial Verdict: How Much Time Is He Facing (RICO trial set for Oct. 5): https://www.complex.com/music/a/tracewilliamcowen/lil-durk-conviction-prison-time\n- Sneakz & Beatz, September 11, 2026 - Lil Durk Found Not Guilty on All Counts: /the-lane/lil-durk-not-guilty-all-counts-murder-for-hire-verdict-2026",
    "publishedAt": "2026-09-11",
