    "slug": "kai-cenat-vivet-first-fashion-show-nyfw-september-12-2026",
    "pillar": "hiphop",
    "heroFocus": "center",
    "title": "Kai Cenat Puts VIVET on the Runway Tonight",
    "headline": "Nine Months Off Stream.\nOne Runway.\nVIVET Walks Tonight.",
    "subhead": "Kai Cenat's clothing brand holds its first fashion show in New York at 8 p.m. ET Saturday, September 12, livestreamed during NYFW. The venue is still a secret. The billboards are not.",
    "description": "Kai Cenat's VIVET holds its first fashion show Sept. 12 at 8 p.m. ET in NYC, livestreamed during NYFW. What we know about the brand he quit streaming to build.",
    "keywords": [
      "Kai Cenat",
      "VIVET",
      "Kai Cenat fashion show",
      "New York Fashion Week 2026",
      "VIVET fashion show livestream",
      "Law Roach",
      "Kai Cenat clothing brand",
      "streamer culture",
      "Slawn",
      "Streamer University",
      "Sneakz and Beatz",
      "PHRHX"
    ],
    "ogHeadline": "VIVET WALKS TONIGHT.",
    "ogAccent": "0F0F0F",
    "heroCredit": "Julian Hamilton / FilmMagic via Getty Images, courtesy Complex",
    "heroCreditUrl": "https://www.complex.com/style/a/markelibert/kai-cenat-vivet-new-york-fashion-week-debut",
    "heroImage": "https://images.complex.com/complex/image/upload/c_crop,h_3789,w_6167,x_934,y_248/g_auto:aoi_2468_1516_1233_758,ar_1.91,c_fill,q_auto,w_1200/sanity-new/qpitjdirluk8nr5ryk90",
    "trendScore": 88,
    "body": "The biggest streamer in the culture is not streaming tonight. He's holding a fashion show. Kai Cenat's VIVET makes its runway debut in New York City on Saturday, September 12 at 8 p.m. ET, inside New York Fashion Week, and the whole thing is being livestreamed for the people who can't get past the door. [Complex](https://www.complex.com/style/a/markelibert/kai-cenat-vivet-new-york-fashion-week-debut) (@Complex) had the invite when [Kai](https://x.com/KaiCenat/status/2093814966646198722) (@KaiCenat) posted it on August 29: \"I Am Happy To Welcome You To VIVET. September 12th.\"\n\nBy Friday night, \"Kai Cenat Debuts VIVET Clothing Brand at New York Fashion Week\" was a trending topic on X. That's the setup. Here's what's actually on the line.\n\n## What we know, and what he's holding back\nThe invitation reads like a mission statement, not a press release: \"Vivet is the story of a collective journey to remove any doubt and unleash the greatness within us all. Through manifestation, knowledge acquisition, discipline, teamwork and having faith, we can move mountains.\" Signed, \"With love, Kai.\" What it doesn't say is where. As of [Dexerto](https://www.dexerto.com/twitch/kai-cenat-vivet-fashion-show-billboards-3407319/)'s (@Dexerto) report on September 9, the venue and the collection are still unannounced. NYFW runs through September 15, so he's landing this in the middle of the week the industry is actually in town.\n\nWhat isn't a secret is the marketing. Minimalist VIVET billboards went up around Manhattan the week of September 8, just the name, the site and the handle, first spotted by [@yoxics](https://x.com/yoxics/status/2097368682041401583) and picked up by Dexerto. Fan accounts are reporting the collection mixes higher-priced pieces with more affordable ones that go on sale right after the show; treat that as unconfirmed until VIVET says it on the stream.\n\n![Kai Cenat on stream ahead of VIVET's first show](https://www.dexerto.com/cdn-image/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/09/kaicenat.jpg \"Kai Cenat via Twitch, courtesy Dexerto|https://www.dexerto.com/twitch/kai-cenat-vivet-fashion-show-billboards-3407319/\")\n\n## The nine months that built this\nThis isn't merch. Kai announced VIVET on December 6, 2025 on his second channel, kai's mind, with a video that showed the design journal and the logo and explained the name: Latin for \"he, she, or it will live forever.\" The next night at the Streamer Awards he said out loud that he wanted to be a fashion designer. Then he disappeared from Twitch for nine months.\n\n!youtube(https://youtu.be/-vK8gk86Z0g)\n\nThe \"I Quit\" video in January was the receipt. Twenty-three minutes of him learning to sew, flying to Italy to study textiles and denim production, and sitting with Law Roach, the stylist who built Zendaya's whole visual language, as his mentor. Complex's [timeline](https://www.complex.com/style/a/mariah-rivera/kai-cenat-vivet-clothing-brand-everything-we-know) has the rest: a custom leather bag drawn on by Slawn in January, Paris Fashion Week Men's with the journal in hand, Pharrell and Future showing love, and Italian footwear designer Mattias Gollin sharing the bedazzled VIVET bag from the \"EBK\" video in July, which set off the guess that he's been building the shoes.\n\nHe came back to streaming July 6 and said the quiet part: the break was for this. Streamer University, the diss track, the Apple event with Speed, all of that was the return tour. Tonight is the thing he actually left for.\n\n![Kai Cenat](https://cassiuslife.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/47/2026/01/17689351368835.jpg \"Gilbert Flores / Getty Images, courtesy Cassius Life|https://cassiuslife.com/1364771/kai-cenat-clothing-brand-vivet-everything-we-know/\")\n\n## Why this matters more than a drop\nStreamers have been handed fashion before. Brands cut them a check, put their name on a capsule, and keep the company. Kai is doing the opposite: he's the creative director, he took the classes, and by [Cassius Life](https://cassiuslife.com/1364771/kai-cenat-clothing-brand-vivet-everything-we-know/)'s (@CassiusLife_) account the thing is his, built with Law Roach in his ear rather than a licensing partner on the cap table. That's the question we ask on every one of these stories: who owns it when the stream ends? Tonight is a 24-year-old from the Bronx answering it on a runway, during the week the fashion establishment is in his city, with his audience watching live because that's the audience he built.\n\nThe critics who called the Paris front-row trip performative in January get their answer at 8 p.m. So does everyone who bought a bootleg VIVET hoodie at Streamer University. If the clothes are real, the biggest streamer alive just became a designer with a built-in customer base no fashion house can buy. If they aren't, the internet will say so in real time. Either way, the livestream is the point: he's making the industry watch on his platform, not theirs.\n\n## Sources\n- Complex - Kai Cenat Announces Vivet's Inaugural Fashion Show in New York City (Aug. 29, 2026): https://www.complex.com/style/a/markelibert/kai-cenat-vivet-new-york-fashion-week-debut\n- Dexerto - Kai Cenat puts Vivet on NYC billboards ahead of brand's first fashion show (Sept. 9, 2026): https://www.dexerto.com/twitch/kai-cenat-vivet-fashion-show-billboards-3407319/\n- Complex - What Is Going on With Kai Cenat's Clothing Brand Vivet? (July 17, 2026): https://www.complex.com/style/a/mariah-rivera/kai-cenat-vivet-clothing-brand-everything-we-know\n- Cassius Life - Kai Cenat Announces Vivet's First Fashion Show & Everything Else We Know (Aug. 31, 2026): https://cassiuslife.com/1364771/kai-cenat-clothing-brand-vivet-everything-we-know/\n- @KaiCenat on X - \"I Am Happy To Welcome You To VIVET. September 12th.\" (Aug. 29, 2026): https://x.com/KaiCenat/status/2093814966646198722\n- X Trending - Kai Cenat Debuts VIVET Clothing Brand at New York Fashion Week (Sept. 11-12, 2026): https://x.com/i/trending/2098107320014385525",
    "publishedAt": "2026-09-12",
    "goLiveAt": "2026-09-12"
