    "title": "APB's Air Jordan 11 Low Drops Friday. It's the Whitaker Group's Next Move.",
    "headline": "Binary Blue. Rust Pink Piping.\nAPB's First Jordan 11 Low Lands September 18.",
    "subhead": "James Whitner's Charlotte shop gets its own 11 Low after A Ma Maniére, Social Status and JAIDE. Premium leather where the mesh goes, $200, SNKRS and APB Friday morning.",
    "description": "APB x Air Jordan 11 Low 'Binary Blue' (IU8266-400) drops Sept. 18, 2026 at $200 via APB and Nike SNKRS. The Whitaker Group shop's first Jordan; a Sail pair follows.",
    "keywords": [
      "APB Air Jordan 11 Low",
      "IU8266-400",
      "APB Jordan 11 Binary Blue",
      "Whitaker Group Jordan",
      "James Whitner",
      "A Ma Maniere Jordan 11",
      "Air Jordan 11 Low September 2026",
      "Sneakz and Beatz",
      "PHRHX"
    ],
    "ogHeadline": "APB x AIR JORDAN 11 LOW.\nFRIDAY. $200.",
    "ogAccent": "1D4ED8",
    "heroCredit": "@beechkicks_ via Sneaker News",
    "heroCreditUrl": "https://sneakernews.com/2026/08/31/apb-air-jordan-11-low-iu8266-400-release-date/",
    "heroImage": "https://sneakernews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/apb-air-jordan-11-low-iu8266-400-release-date-2.jpg",
    "trendScore": 82,
    "body": "James Whitner has spent a decade turning a handful of Black-owned boutiques into the most consistent collab machine in the Jordan ecosystem. A Ma Maniére got the 3, the 1, the 4 and the 5. Social Status got the 6 Low. JAIDE, the women's line, has an 11 Low landing the same week. Now it's APB's turn. The Charlotte store's first Jordan, an Air Jordan 11 Low in \"Binary Blue,\" releases Friday, September 18. [Sneaker News](https://sneakernews.com/2026/08/31/apb-air-jordan-11-low-iu8266-400-release-date/) and [Sneaker Files](https://www.sneakerfiles.com/apb-air-jordan-11-low-pack/) have it confirmed; the in-hand shots came from [@beechkicks_](https://www.instagram.com/beechkicks_/).\n\n## The shoe\n\nStyle code IU8266-400. Binary Blue/Rust Pink-Sail-Steel. The biggest change is material: the ballistic mesh that defines every 11 Low is gone, replaced with premium leather, which turns the shoe from a summer sneaker into something you'd wear with a jacket. Salmon-pink piping traces the panels and the patent mudguard. $200 per Sneaker News; Sneaker Files lists $205. APB's site and Nike SNKRS, 10 a.m. ET.\n\nA second pair, Sail with Rust Pink and Binary Blue flipped, is coming later with its own style code. Sneaker Files has both together.\n\n![APB x Air Jordan 11 Low \"Binary Blue\" in hand](https://sneakernews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/apb-air-jordan-11-low-iu8266-400-release-date-1.jpg \"@beechkicks_ via Sneaker News|https://sneakernews.com/2026/08/31/apb-air-jordan-11-low-iu8266-400-release-date/\")\n\n## Why the 11 Low matters here\n\nJordan almost never gives the 11 to collaborators. The silhouette is the brand's December cash register and it protects it. A handful of 11 Low collabs exist and most of them are recent; giving one to APB, the smallest name in the Whitaker portfolio, says the group has earned the kind of trust Jordan doesn't extend to new partners. Sneaker News frames APB as \"a herald of what's to come,\" with a Whitaker Group 4 already on the books for 2027.\n\nThat's the ownership story. Whitner built the Whitaker Group as a Black-owned retail company in a business where Black shops usually get allocation, not authorship. Four stores with their own Jordan collabs in one calendar year is a level of access that used to belong to Kith and Union alone.\n\n![APB x Air Jordan 11 Low pack](https://www.sneakerfiles.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/apb-air-jordan-11-low-pack-2026.jpg \"Sneaker Files|https://www.sneakerfiles.com/apb-air-jordan-11-low-pack/\")\n\n## How to get it\n\nAPB will run its own release, and SNKRS gets a general allocation the same morning. The JAIDE 11 Low \"Fiberglass\" is a raffle release the same weekend through JAIDE, A Ma Maniére, Social Status and APB, so if you're in Charlotte, Atlanta or Pittsburgh, the store lines are going to be one long weekend. Blue, leather, a 11 Low with a story: this is the one from the September calendar that ages.\n\n## Sources\n- [APB x Air Jordan 11 Low IU8266-400 Release Date](https://sneakernews.com/2026/08/31/apb-air-jordan-11-low-iu8266-400-release-date/) — Sneaker News (@SneakerNews), Aug. 31, 2026 (updated Sept. 2026)\n- [APB x Air Jordan 11 Low Pack](https://www.sneakerfiles.com/apb-air-jordan-11-low-pack/) — Sneaker Files (@Sneaker_Files), Sept. 2026\n- [APB x Air Jordan 11 Low \"Binary Blue\"](https://sneakerbardetroit.com/apb-air-jordan-11-low-binary-blue/) — Sneaker Bar Detroit (@SBDsneakers), Sept. 2026\n",
