    "ogHeadline": "\"FREEDOM. FREEDOM. FREEDOM.\"\nDURK SPEAKS.\nSTILL IN CUSTODY.",
    "ogAccent": "1B3A6B",
    "heroCredit": "Kamil Krzaczynski / USA TODAY Sports via Reuters Connect, courtesy HotNewHipHop",
    "heroCreditUrl": "https://www.hotnewhiphop.com/1009469-lil-durk-breaks-silence-murder-for-hire-acquittal",
    "heroImage": "https://www.hotnewhiphop.com/imgprst/2292x1200-fit-81-auto/2026/09/Lil-Durk-Breaks-Silence-Murder-For-Hire-Acquittal-scaled.jpg",
    "heroFocus": "center",
    "trendScore": 92,
    "body": "Lil Durk's first words after the verdict were not about the verdict. \"Against all odds, we're stronger together,\" he wrote on [Instagram](https://www.instagram.com/p/DdNQy-phZbn/) (@lildurk) Saturday night, under a photo of his legal team. \"Allah doesn't make mistakes. I feel all the love and positive energy. Now let me be free to help save our kids and bring unity back to our communities. I couldn't have made it this far without my family, my lawyers, and supporters. Freedom. Freedom. Freedom.\"\n\nThat's the whole statement, per [HotNewHipHop](https://www.hotnewhiphop.com/1009469-lil-durk-breaks-silence-murder-for-hire-acquittal) (@HotNewHipHop), which had it first Sunday morning. Nothing about the jury, nothing about the prosecutors, nothing about the two years. We [covered the acquittal Friday](/the-lane/lil-durk-not-guilty-all-counts-murder-for-hire-verdict-2026) and [Brian Steel's victory lap](/the-lane/brian-steel-mvp-hip-hop-reacts-lil-durk-not-guilty-rico-october-5-2026) Saturday. This is Durk himself, and the word he chose to say three times is the one thing he still doesn't have.\n\n## \"Let me be free\" is doing a lot of work\n\nRead the sentence again. Not \"I'm free.\" \"Let me be free.\" Durk is still in federal custody, and [HotNewHipHop](https://www.hotnewhiphop.com/1009415-lil-durk-remain-custody-not-guilty-verdict) laid out why: the racketeering and firearms counts the court severed from the Los Angeles case are set for trial October 5, tied to a 2022 Chicago murder and a 2019 Atlanta shooting. Before that, prosecutors and the defense will fight over bond. So the post reads less like a celebration and more like an opening argument to the next judge, delivered to 15 million followers. Save our kids. Unity. Communities. That's the man he's asking the court to see in three weeks.\n\nHis wife got there first. India Royale posted a photo of Durk kissing their daughter Willow on Friday night with three words, \"Thank you GOD,\" per [Complex](https://www.complex.com/music/a/jaelaniturnerwilliams/india-royale-lil-durk-murder-hire-trial-acquittal) (@Complex). She sat through every day of the trial from August 24 on.\n\n![India Royale and Lil Durk](https://images.complex.com/complex/image/upload/c_crop,h_906,w_1220,x_475,y_1/g_auto:aoi_866_126_244_181,ar_1.91,c_fill,q_auto,w_1200/sanity-new/yuiypaxjmqejytddtfuy \"Jeff Kravitz / FilmMagic via Complex|https://www.complex.com/music/a/jaelaniturnerwilliams/india-royale-lil-durk-murder-hire-trial-acquittal\")\n\n## The photo is the message\n\nDurk didn't post himself. He posted Steel and Drew Findling, the two lawyers who have now beaten the feds for Young Thug and for him inside two years, with Marissa Goldberg and Christy O'Connor in the frame. NBA guard Quinn Cook put an OTF chain on Findling's neck this weekend, which tells you how the culture is scoring this: the defense bar is the new front office. [50 Cent called Findling](https://variety.com/2026/music/news/lil-durk-acquitted-murder-for-hire-trial-1236859311/) the billion-dollar lawyer. Thug took a bow for lending Steel. Everybody wants a piece of the win.\n\nNot everybody. [Young Thug spent Saturday](https://www.hotnewhiphop.com/1009449-young-thug-disses-otf-jam-otf-vonni-lil-durk-verdict) going at OTF Jam and OTF Vonni, the two cooperators who took the stand against Durk. [6ix9ine](https://www.complex.com/music/a/jaelaniturnerwilliams/6ix9ine-taunts-lil-durk-verdict-custody-acquittal) went ahead with his \"Lil Durk Going Away Party\" anyway and posted that Durk is \"still in prison.\" And [Meek Mill told his followers to mute DJ Akademiks](https://www.complex.com/music/a/treyalston/meek-mill-dj-akademiks-lil-durk-verdict) over the trial coverage, which Ak shrugged off. Durk's statement floats above all of it, which is the point of it.\n\n## What he's actually asking for\n\nTwo years in MDC. A three-week trial where the government's own witnesses were his own crew. Five counts, five not-guilties. And the next hearing is about whether he can go home before the next trial starts. \"Freedom. Freedom. Freedom.\" is a prayer, a hashtag, and a bond motion in three words. The court answers in October. The timeline already has.\n\n## Sources\n- HotNewHipHop - Lil Durk Breaks His Silence On His Murder-For-Hire Acquittal (Sept. 13, 2026): https://www.hotnewhiphop.com/1009469-lil-durk-breaks-silence-murder-for-hire-acquittal\n- @lildurk on Instagram (Sept. 12, 2026): https://www.instagram.com/p/DdNQy-phZbn/\n- Hip Hop Vibe - Lil Durk releases first statement since not guilty verdict (Sept. 12, 2026): https://hip-hopvibe.com/news/lil-durk-releases-first-statement-since-not-guilty-verdict-in-murder-for-hire-trial/\n- Complex - India Royale Breaks Her Silence After Husband Lil Durk's Acquittal (Sept. 12, 2026): https://www.complex.com/music/a/jaelaniturnerwilliams/india-royale-lil-durk-murder-hire-trial-acquittal\n- HotNewHipHop - Lil Durk Will Remain In Custody After Not Guilty Murder-For-Hire Verdict (Sept. 12, 2026): https://www.hotnewhiphop.com/1009415-lil-durk-remain-custody-not-guilty-verdict\n- HotNewHipHop - Young Thug Disses OTF Jam & OTF Vonni After Lil Durk Verdict (Sept. 12, 2026): https://www.hotnewhiphop.com/1009449-young-thug-disses-otf-jam-otf-vonni-lil-durk-verdict\n- Complex - Meek Mill Urges Fans to 'Mute' DJ Akademiks After Lil Durk Verdict (Sept. 12, 2026): https://www.complex.com/music/a/treyalston/meek-mill-dj-akademiks-lil-durk-verdict\n- Complex - 6ix9ine Taunts Lil Durk for Remaining in Custody After Acquittal (Sept. 12, 2026): https://www.complex.com/music/a/jaelaniturnerwilliams/6ix9ine-taunts-lil-durk-verdict-custody-acquittal\n- Variety - Lil Durk Acquitted in Murder-for-Hire Trial (Sept. 11, 2026): https://variety.com/2026/music/news/lil-durk-acquitted-murder-for-hire-trial-1236859311/\n",
