    "headline": "The 'Free Durk' Shirt\nAged Perfectly.",
    "subhead": "Ye sat with Durk's family during a cooperator's testimony in August, posed with Doodie Lo in a 'Free Durk' tee, and was one of the first names on the timeline when the not-guilty verdict dropped. Chicago loyalty, on the record.",
    "description": "Ye showed up to Lil Durk's federal trial on Aug. 27 in a 'Free Durk' shirt, sat with the family, then posted 'Lil Durk is not guilty on ALL COUNTS' the moment the verdict broke Sept. 11. Sneakz & Beatz on the Ye-Durk arc, from 'Jonah' to the courthouse.",
    "publishedAt": "2026-09-13",
    "goLiveAt": "2026-09-13",
    "keywords": [
      "Ye Lil Durk",
      "Kanye West Lil Durk trial",
      "Free Durk shirt",
      "Ye courthouse",
      "Ye Doodie Lo",
      "Jonah Donda",
      "Ye 2026",
      "Kanye West news",
      "Sneakz and Beatz",
      "PHRHX"
    ],
    "ogHeadline": "YE SAID FREE DURK.\nTHE JURY AGREED.",
    "ogAccent": "1F3A5F",
    "heroCredit": "Billboard",
    "heroCreditUrl": "https://www.billboard.com/music/rb-hip-hop/ye-lil-durk-support-trial-1236326688/",
    "trendScore": 88,
    "heroFocus": "center top",
    "body": "Every rapper posted when the verdict came in. One of them had already put his body in the building.\n\nOn August 27, Ye walked into the downtown Los Angeles federal courthouse in all black and sat through OTF Jam's testimony, the prosecution's cooperating witness, next to Durk's family. Outside, he posed with Doodie Lo holding up a \"Free Durk\" T-shirt. Doodie Lo's caption: \"Ye we love and respect you for showing up at our darkest times.\" [Billboard](https://www.billboard.com/music/rb-hip-hop/ye-lil-durk-support-trial-1236326688/) covered the appearance that afternoon.\n\nFifteen days later a jury cleared Durk on all five counts. Ye's post on X was one line: \"Lil Durk is not guilty on ALL COUNTS.\" It traveled because of the courthouse photo, not the caps lock.\n\n## Why it landed different\nThe Ye-Durk connection is real music, not a mutual follow. \"Jonah\" on Donda in 2021 had Durk and Vory carrying the hook about loss. Durk showed up on the Vultures title track. They shared a Cardi B record in 2022. Two Chicago men a generation apart, and the older one showed up to the younger one's worst month without a camera crew.\n\nThat's the version of Ye this audience wants to talk about, and it's worth separating from the other one. HotNewHipHop spent its Friday livestream asking whether Ye's stadium run is a redemption or a ruse, and the criticism of his last three years hasn't gone anywhere. Both things are on the record. Report both.\n\n## What's still ahead\nDurk stays in custody until the October 5 racketeering trial. The Bully tour keeps moving: Houston on Halloween (on sale now), Arlington November 7, Phoenix November 21, all registration or on-sale through tour.yeezy.com and the venues. If Durk is out by the fall dates, a Chicago moment on one of those stages writes itself. Nobody's promised that. We're noting it.\n\n## Sources\n- Billboard, August 27, 2026 - Kanye West Supports Lil Durk at Chicago Rapper's Trial: https://www.billboard.com/music/rb-hip-hop/ye-lil-durk-support-trial-1236326688/\n- Complex, September 11, 2026 - Kanye West, and More React to Verdict in Lil Durk's Murder-for-Hire Case: https://www.complex.com/music/a/jaelaniturnerwilliams/celebrities-react-lil-durk-verdict\n- HotNewHipHop, September 12, 2026 - Are Ye & Jay-Z's Concerts Redemptions Or Ruses? (HNHH Live): https://www.hotnewhiphop.com/1009419-ye-jay-z-concerts-redemptions-ruses\n- Billboard, September 1, 2026 - Kanye West Stadium Shows in Dallas, Houston & Phoenix Announced: https://www.billboard.com/music/rb-hip-hop/kanye-west-us-tour-stadium-shows-dallas-houston-phoenix-1236331481/\n"
