    "trendScore": 55,
    "heroFocus": "center",
    "body": "Bouclé is the looped, nubby wool you find on a Chanel jacket or a $4,000 armchair. Jordan Brand just put it on a 1 Low and priced it like a 1 Low.\n\n## The details\nOfficial images ran on [Sneaker News](https://sneakernews.com/2026/09/13/air-jordan-1-low-boucle-iz6154-121/) September 13. Style code IZ6154-121, women's sizing, $125, Fall/Winter 2026 with no firm date yet. The bouclé wraps the heel panel and collar. Small metallic silver rectangles carrying the Wings logo sit on the lateral side near the tail of the Swoosh. Light blue on the toe, forefoot and eyelets with white contrast stitch, a maroon Swoosh and lining, metallic silver Jumpman on the tongue, script branding on the insoles.\n\n## The idea\nSneaker News read it as a luxury-accessory theme, in the lane Vans has been working with its Souvenir series. Jordan Brand has been playing with textiles on the women's 1 Low all year, and this is the most on-the-nose version: a material you associate with furniture and couture, on the entry-price Jordan.\n\n## Who it's for\nThis isn't a retro in the strict sense; it's a women's-exclusive colorway on the OG Low block, and at $125 it's the cheapest 1 on the fall calendar. If the 1 Low 'Last Dance at the Garden' on September 26 is the one for the collector, this is the one for the person who wears her 1s every day and wants a pair nobody else on the train has.\n\n## Sources\n- Sneaker News, Sept. 13, 2026 — Jordan Brand turns to luxury goods with the Air Jordan 1 Low 'Bouclé': https://sneakernews.com/2026/09/13/air-jordan-1-low-boucle-iz6154-121/\n- Just Fresh Kicks, Sept. 14, 2026 — Air Jordan 1 Low 'Bouclé' releases Fall/Winter 2026: https://justfreshkicks.com/air-jordan-1-low-boucle-iz6154-121/\n"
