    "slug": "papoose-jezebel-remy-ma-claressa-shields-divorce-hearing-september-11-2026",
    "pillar": "hiphop",
    "title": "Papoose Dropped 'Jezebel' the Same Day as the Divorce Hearing",
    "headline": "Same Day as Court.\nHe Dropped a Record.",
    "subhead": "Papoose answered two Remy Ma diss songs with one of his own, released September 11 while the two were in a virtual divorce hearing. Claressa Shields is defending it. Remy is teasing the next one. Nobody has signed anything.",
    "description": "Papoose released 'Jezebel' Sept. 11, the day of a divorce hearing with Remy Ma. Claressa Shields defended the song; Remy teased 'Why I Get Married.'",
    "publishedAt": "2026-09-14",
    "goLiveAt": "2026-09-14",
    "keywords": [
      "Papoose Jezebel",
      "Remy Ma Papoose divorce",
      "Claressa Shields Remy Ma",
      "Papoose diss track",
      "Remy Ma Why I Get Married",
      "Papoose Remy Ma beef",
      "Remy Ma WYFL",
      "Papoose ghostwriting Remy Ma",
      "Sneakz and Beatz",
      "PHRHX",
      "Black-owned media"
    ],
    "ogHeadline": "SAME DAY AS COURT.\nHE DROPPED A RECORD.",
    "ogAccent": "B3001B",
    "heroCredit": "Terry Shropshire for rolling out",
    "heroCreditUrl": "https://rollingout.com/2026/09/11/papoose-releases-diss-track-jezebel-aimed-at-remy-ma/",
    "heroImage": "https://rollingout.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/0FB51926-E046-4CDB-A49B-922ACC94B842-scaled-e1789170427317.jpg",
    "trendScore": 85,
    "heroFocus": "center",
    "body": "Black Love, the reality show, ran for years on the premise that these two were the exception. The divorce is now being litigated on wax, in real time, with a boxer in the middle.\n\n## What dropped\nPapoose released \"Jezebel\" with a video on Friday, September 11, per [rolling out](https://rollingout.com/2026/09/11/papoose-releases-diss-track-jezebel-aimed-at-remy-ma/), which reports he cut the song and shot the visual in under 24 hours. [HotNewHipHop](https://www.hotnewhiphop.com/1009445-papoose-remy-ma-beef-new-music-video) notes the same day carried a virtual divorce hearing between him and Remy Ma. He never says her name. He doesn't have to. The record claims he treated her well, that she cheated and he kept quiet for their daughter's sake, that her cheating accusations against him are lies, and that he ghostwrote for her. The line doing the rounds: \"When you was locked up, I brought you food, sent you mail.\"\n\n!youtube(https://youtu.be/sceez20rWjM)\n\n## Why it's a response, not an opener\nRemy fired first. \"W.Y.F.L.\" (Why You F***ing Lying) went at Papoose over the songwriting claims and his relationship with Claressa Shields. \"Wanna Go\" followed, timed to land right before Shields' August fight. Papoose's lawyers sent a cease-and-desist over both, per rolling out. Then on September 10 Remy posted a clip riding to her Millyz record \"Say Yea,\" hashtagged \"NOBODYYYY want Ya Man,\" named the court date, and told him to sign the papers and \"prove\" his love to Shields, per [rolling out](https://rollingout.com/2026/09/12/remy-ma-ultimatum-to-papoose/). That post pulled 3,400 comments in three hours. \"Free Remy\" trended in the replies.\n\n![Papoose with Claressa Shields](https://rollingout.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/0FB51926-E046-4CDB-A49B-922ACC94B842-scaled-e1789170427317.jpg \"Terry Shropshire for rolling out|https://rollingout.com/2026/09/11/papoose-releases-diss-track-jezebel-aimed-at-remy-ma/\")\n\n## Shields is in it now\nClaressa Shields went on her livestream and told everybody mad at \"Jezebel\" to get off it, called it a good song, and counted the three diss tracks she says have been aimed at her and her man. On X she called Remy, Alycia Baumgardner and Amanda Serrano \"3 loser b***hes linking up,\" per [The Shade Room](https://theshaderoom.com/claressa-shields-appears-to-call-remy-ma-names-responding-to-fan-papoose/). Earlier in the week Remy had posted a sandwich in a panini press captioned \"Mr. and Mrs. Panini.\" This is where the discourse is.\n\n## The part nobody can settle\nAngela Yee claimed Remy filed to dismiss the divorce and a judge denied it; Remy appeared to deny that on Instagram, per HNHH. Each side says the other is dragging it. Remy's next record, \"Why I Get Married\" with Keke Wyatt, is teased for later this month. The comment consensus on Papoose's video, captured by rolling out, was not kind: \"pap going out sad,\" and one that summed up the week in hip-hop, \"free durk!!! we don't wanna hear this.\"\n\n## Why it matters\nThe Remy-and-Pap brand was loyalty: he wrote to her through a six-year bid, she came home to him, they built a franchise on it. The same story is now the ammunition. Papoose is the one who used to talk about carrying her; on \"Jezebel\" it's an invoice. The songwriting accusation is the one with a shelf life. If he really did pen for her, it rewrites the Remy catalog. If he didn't, it's the most damaging thing a New York lyricist can say about another, and he said it on a hook.\n\n## Sources\n- rolling out, Sept. 11, 2026 — Papoose releases diss track 'Jezebel' aimed at Remy Ma: https://rollingout.com/2026/09/11/papoose-releases-diss-track-jezebel-aimed-at-remy-ma/\n- rolling out, Sept. 12, 2026 — Remy Ma's ultimatum to Papoose has the internet taking sides: https://rollingout.com/2026/09/12/remy-ma-ultimatum-to-papoose/\n- HotNewHipHop, Sept. 12, 2026 — Papoose & Remy Ma go at each other after Pap's new music video: https://www.hotnewhiphop.com/1009445-papoose-remy-ma-beef-new-music-video\n- The Shade Room, Sept. 2026 — Claressa Shields appears to call Remy Ma names: https://theshaderoom.com/claressa-shields-appears-to-call-remy-ma-names-responding-to-fan-papoose/\n- Black America Web, Sept. 13, 2026 — Papoose continues pen-pushing accusations on 'Jezebel': https://blackamericaweb.com/2026/09/13/papoose-accusations-remy-ma-diss-track-jezebel/\n"
