    "pillar": "gaming",
    "title": "Cyberpunk 2077 Leaves Game Pass Today. Where It Lives Now",
    "headline": "Night City\nLeft Game Pass.",
    "subhead": "September 15 is the day Cyberpunk 2077 drops off Xbox Game Pass. Your save carries over if you buy it, Battle.net is coming later this year, and the next three Cyberpunk dates are already on the calendar.",
    "description": "Cyberpunk 2077 leaves Xbox Game Pass on Sept. 15, 2026. Where to buy it, whether your save survives, and the next dates: Witcher 3 Remastered and Edgerunners 2.",
    "publishedAt": "2026-09-15",
    "goLiveAt": "2026-09-15",
    "keywords": [
      "Cyberpunk 2077 Game Pass",
      "Cyberpunk 2077 leaving Game Pass",
      "Cyberpunk 2077 where to buy",
      "Cyberpunk 2077 save transfer",
      "Cyberpunk 2077 Battle.net",
      "Edgerunners 2 October 20",
      "Witcher 3 Remastered",
      "Sneakz and Beatz",
      "PHRHX",
      "Black-owned media"
    ],
    "ogHeadline": "NIGHT CITY\nLEFT GAME PASS.",
    "ogAccent": "F2C94C",
    "heroCredit": "CD Projekt Red",
    "heroCreditUrl": "https://www.cyberpunk.net/",
    "trendScore": 78,
    "heroFocus": "center",
    "body": "If you've been running Night City on a subscription, today's the day it stops working. Cyberpunk 2077 leaves Xbox Game Pass on September 15, console and cloud. Nothing dramatic, just the end of a rotation. Here's the practical version.\n\n## Your save\nBuy the game on the same Xbox account and your save is still there. Game Pass saves live on your account, not on the sub. That includes Phantom Liberty progress if you bought the expansion separately, which you had to, because the expansion was never part of the Game Pass deal.\n\n## Where to buy it\nBase game and the Ultimate Edition (base plus Phantom Liberty) are on Xbox, PlayStation, Steam, GOG, Epic, and Switch 2. The 2.x updates that fixed the game are in every version. And the fourth PC storefront is coming: CD Projekt confirmed at BlizzCon that the base game, Phantom Liberty, and the Ultimate Edition land on Battle.net later this year, no date, no price yet.\n\n## The next three dates\nThe Cyberpunk trading card game's beta week wraps Thursday, September 17, ahead of a November 6 release. The Witcher 3 Remastered lands September 29 as a free upgrade for owners, and pre-ordering its Songs of the Past expansion on Battle.net gets you a Geralt skin in Diablo 4. And Cyberpunk: Edgerunners 2 hits Netflix October 20. The game leaving a subscription isn't the story; the universe getting bigger is.\n\n## Sources\n- CD Projekt Red press center, Sept. 13, 2026, Cyberpunk 2077 comes to Battle.net: https://press.cdprojektred.com/en/news/1847/cyberpunk-2077-comes-to-battle-net\n- Cyberpunk 2077 official site, editions and platforms: https://www.cyberpunk.net/\n- CD Projekt Red press center, Edgerunners 2 trailer and release window: https://press.cdprojektred.com/en/news/1831/cyberpunk-edgerunners-2-gets-new-trailer-and-fall-2026-release-window\n"
