    "trendScore": 86,
    "heroFocus": "center",
    "body": "First, the correction. On September 10 we told you Summer Madness 15 was September 21 in London. That was 2025's card. This year's is real, it's confirmed, and it's twelve days out.\n\n## The card\nURL Summer Madness XVI, Sunday, September 27, Variety Playhouse in Atlanta's Little Five Points. Doors at 2pm, show at 3pm, 18 and over, tickets on AXS. The venue's listing names Tay Roc, Ill Will, Rum Nitty, and Chess, \"and many others.\" The matchup URL announced itself, on August 24: Tay Roc vs Rum Nitty, \"dropping exclusively on the URLTV app.\"\n\n## Why Roc vs Nitty\nTay Roc is URL's franchise player, the most-booked battler in the league's history, gun bars and pace nobody matches. Rum Nitty is the pen, a puncher whose schemes get replayed frame by frame the next morning. They've circled each other for years. Putting it at the top of the biggest card of the year, in Atlanta, is Smack telling you which era he thinks this is.\n\n## Why Atlanta\nSummer Madness has lived in New York and gone overseas. Bringing it to the city that runs rap right now, with a Black-owned league on a Sunday afternoon, is a statement about where the audience is. Variety Playhouse is a 1,000-cap room, which means it sells out, which means the app is where most of us watch.\n\n## Before you go\nCards change late. Ill Will and Chess don't have named opponents in the listing yet. Check @urltv for the full slate the week of, and get on the app if you're not in the building.\n\n## Sources\n- AXS, URL Summer Madness, Variety Playhouse, Atlanta, Sun. Sept. 27, 2026: https://www.axs.com/events/1576515/url-summer-madness-tickets\n- Ultimate Rap League on X, Aug. 24, 2026, Tay Roc vs Rum Nitty, Summer Madness XVI: https://x.com/urltv/status/2091952484390498313\n- Ultimate Rap League on X: https://x.com/urltv\n"
