    "heroFocus": "center",
    "body": "The anime ended. The franchise is about to tell you it didn't. Toho Animation confirmed on September 13 that a new My Hero Academia project will be announced on September 20.\n\n## The stream\n\"All Might Nippon YouTube Special Edition: 10th Anniversary Midterm Report,\" live on Toho Animation's YouTube channel at 6pm Japan time, which is 2am Pacific and 5am Eastern on Sunday, September 20. Hosts are Daiki Yamashita, the voice of Izuku Midoriya, and Nobuhiko Okamoto, Katsuki Bakugo. All Might Nippon was the show's official web radio program through all eight seasons; this is the video version.\n\n## What \"new project\" could mean\nNobody knows and the smart move is not to guess on air. The 10th-anniversary program already lists 15 initiatives, including a free streaming marathon, a U.S. concert tour that opened September 12, and the Switch 2 launch of All's Justice. The official page keeps saying more special projects are coming. The anime wrapped with season 8, so anything new is either a film, a spinoff, or something the manga's ending left room for.\n\n## Why the timing works\nMHA turned a generation of American kids into anime fans between 2016 and 2020, the same window a lot of this audience started watching with their own kids. A tenth-anniversary swing is aimed at both. Set an alarm or watch the replay; either way, Sunday is when you find out.\n\n## Sources\n- Anime Corner, My Hero Academia to announce new project as part of 10th anniversary on September 20: https://animecorner.me/my-hero-academia-to-announce-new-project-as-part-of-10th-anniversary-on-september-20/\n- ComicBook.com, My Hero Academia confirms date for next major 10th anniversary reveal: https://comicbook.com/anime/news/my-hero-academia-confirms-date-for-next-major-10th-anniversary-reveal/\n- Variety, My Hero Academia marks 10th anniversary with free streaming marathon: https://variety.com/2026/tv/news/my-hero-academia-10th-anniversary-free-streaming-more-episode-1236706112/\n"
