    "trendScore": 86,
    "body": "An HBCU Jordan that drops in the school's city first, at a neighborhood retailer in Northeast DC, before the rest of the country gets a shot. That's the order of operations we ask for and almost never get.\n\n## The details\nPer [Sneaker News](https://sneakernews.com/2026/09/16/air-jordan-1-retro-low-og-howard-bison-ix8478-410/) (Sept. 16, updated Sept. 17), the Air Jordan 1 Low OG \"Howard University,\" IX8478-410, Midnight Navy/Multi-Color, opened a SNKRS Pass reservation window on Wednesday, Sept. 17, 5:30 to 6:30 p.m. ET, Washington, D.C. only. Winners pick up Sept. 22 at DTLR Rhode Island Place, 1060 Brentwood Rd NE. Wide release follows Oct. 1 on Nike SNKRS. Price is listed at $155 in the Where-to-Buy widget while the article copy says \"likely\" $140; treat $155 as the working number until Nike posts it. [Sneaker Bar Detroit](https://sneakerbardetroit.com/air-jordan-1-low-og-howard-university-2026/) carries the same date.\n\n![Air Jordan 1 Low OG Howard University, official image](https://sneakernews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/air-jordan-1-howard-4.jpg \"Sneaker News / Nike|https://sneakernews.com/2026/09/16/air-jordan-1-retro-low-og-howard-bison-ix8478-410/\")\n\n## The build\nExposed-stitch Swoosh, red and white worked through the Bison palette, and \"Howard Bison\" branding stamped on the heel. In-hand shots credited to [@ladylondon](https://www.instagram.com/ladylondon/) show the navy reading deeper than the renders. This is a proper OG Low, not a Low '86 or a golf cut.\n\n![Air Jordan 1 Low OG Howard University, in hand](https://sneakernews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/air-jordan-1-retro-low-og-howard-bison-ix8478-410-2.jpg \"@ladylondon via Sneaker News|https://sneakernews.com/2026/09/16/air-jordan-1-retro-low-og-howard-bison-ix8478-410/\")\n\n## The lineage\nHoward got a player-exclusive AJ1 in 2023 that never released. Nike turned that into an inverse public colorway in 2024 (HQ2993-100). This is the third chapter, and the first one where the school's own colorway hits general release. Nike's broader HBCU program, the Yardrunners Air Max 95 pack last year, covered Spelman, Morehouse, FAMU and Norfolk State; Howard gets the Jordan.\n\n## The read\nThe DTLR detail is the whole story. A DC-only pass, picked up at a DTLR in Northeast, for a Howard shoe, before SNKRS opens it to the bots. That's a release structured around who the shoe is for. Jordan Brand does not do this often enough. When it does, say so, and show up Oct. 1 if you missed the pass.\n\n## Sources\n- Sneaker News, Sept. 16, 2026 (updated Sept. 17), Air Jordan 1 Low OG \"Howard Bison\" IX8478-410: https://sneakernews.com/2026/09/16/air-jordan-1-retro-low-og-howard-bison-ix8478-410/\n- Sneaker Bar Detroit, Sept. 18, 2026, Air Jordan 1 Low OG \"Howard University\": https://sneakerbardetroit.com/air-jordan-1-low-og-howard-university-2026/\n- House of Heat, Air Jordan 1 Low OG \"Howard University\" IX8478-410: https://houseofheat.co/jordan/2026-air-jordan-1-low-og-howard-university-ix8478-410\n",
