    "title": "A Typhoon Just Killed the Last Day of Tokyo Game Show's 'Longest Five Days'",
    "headline": "TGS Promised Five Days.\nDujuan Made It Four.",
    "subhead": "CESA canceled all Monday, Sept. 21 programming at Tokyo Game Show 2026 as Typhoon Dujuan closed in. The 30th-anniversary show's whole hook was its first five-day run. Ticket holders get refunds; some stages move online.",
    "description": "Tokyo Game Show 2026 canceled its final day (Sept. 21) due to Typhoon Dujuan, announced Sept. 19. The first five-day TGS ends at four; Monday tickets refunded, select stages go digital.",
    "keywords": [
      "Tokyo Game Show 2026 canceled",
      "TGS 2026 typhoon",
      "Typhoon Dujuan Tokyo Game Show",
      "TGS 2026 final day canceled",
      "Tokyo Game Show refunds",
      "CESA TGS 2026",
      "TGS 30th anniversary",
      "Makuhari Messe typhoon",
      "Sneakz and Beatz",
      "PHRHX",
      "Black-owned media"
    ],
    "ogHeadline": "TGS PROMISED FIVE DAYS.\nDUJUAN MADE IT FOUR.",
    "ogAccent": "1565C0",
    "heroImage": "https://kotaku.com/app/uploads/2026/09/GettyImages-2236883946-e1789839807465.jpg",
    "heroCredit": "Getty Images via Kotaku",
    "heroCreditUrl": "https://kotaku.com/typhoon-dujuan-forces-tokyo-game-show-2026-to-shut-down-a-day-early-2000735879",
    "trendScore": 66,
    "body": "The [30th-anniversary pitch](https://sneakzandbeatz.com/the-lane/tokyo-game-show-2026-30th-anniversary-five-days-759-exhibitors-xbox-broadcast-september-17) was \"The Longest Five Days of Nonstop Play.\" Nature had notes.\n\n## What happened\nOn Saturday, Sept. 19, per [Kotaku](https://kotaku.com/typhoon-dujuan-forces-tokyo-game-show-2026-to-shut-down-a-day-early-2000735879), CESA canceled the entire final day of Tokyo Game Show 2026, Monday, Sept. 21, as Typhoon No. 25, internationally named Dujuan, approached the Kanto region. [Anime News Network](https://www.animenewsnetwork.com/news/2026-09-19/tokyo-game-show-2026-cancels-final-day-on-monday-due-to-approaching-typhoon/.241974) reports the organizer cited strengthening wind and rain from Monday afternoon and the risk of transportation shutdowns around Makuhari Messe in Chiba. Sunday, Sept. 20 went ahead with a warning that some facilities and content could be modified for safety, per [GosuGamers](https://www.gosugamers.net/entertainment/news/79210-tokyo-game-show-2026-cancelled-on-last-day-due-to-approaching-typhoon-dujuan).\n\n## What ticket holders get\nFull refunds for Sept. 21 tickets. Select Monday stage presentations move to digital livestreams. Exhibitors with Monday-only slots lose them; the public days that drove the five-day gimmick just became a standard weekend.\n\n![Tokyo Game Show 2026, Anime News Network](https://www.animenewsnetwork.com/thumbnails/crop600x315gI5/cms/news.9/241974/0a6a3619.jpg \"Anime News Network|https://www.animenewsnetwork.com/news/2026-09-19/tokyo-game-show-2026-cancels-final-day-on-monday-due-to-approaching-typhoon/.241974\")\n\n## The week it still had\nThe show delivered before the storm did. Xbox's Thursday broadcast gave us [Physint's lead](https://sneakzandbeatz.com/the-lane/physint-bill-skarsgard-lead-kojima-xbox-tokyo-game-show-poster-od-knock-2026) and the [MW4 campaign trailer](https://sneakzandbeatz.com/the-lane/call-of-duty-modern-warfare-4-campaign-trailer-mads-mikkelsen-the-archer-october-23-2026). Capcom ran its Spotlight. Sony's [300-inch GTA 6 theater](https://sneakzandbeatz.com/the-lane/gta-6-tokyo-game-show-2026-playstation-300-inch-theater-floor-haptics-free-shirt-take-two-meeting) did its business through the weekend. What Monday loses is mostly the tail: late stage shows, last-day floor traffic, and the record attendance number CESA was hoping to print for the anniversary.\n\n## The read\nFive days was always a marketing number more than a programming need; the show has run its business-then-public rhythm at four for decades. Losing Monday to a typhoon is bad luck, not a failure. But it does mean the 30th TGS goes in the books as the one that promised the longest run in its history and closed early. Next year's tagline will be shorter.\n\n## Sources\n- Kotaku, Sept. 19, 2026, Typhoon Dujuan forces TGS to shut a day early: https://kotaku.com/typhoon-dujuan-forces-tokyo-game-show-2026-to-shut-down-a-day-early-2000735879\n- Anime News Network, Sept. 19, 2026, TGS cancels final day: https://www.animenewsnetwork.com/news/2026-09-19/tokyo-game-show-2026-cancels-final-day-on-monday-due-to-approaching-typhoon/.241974\n- GosuGamers, Sept. 19, 2026, TGS last day canceled: https://www.gosugamers.net/entertainment/news/79210-tokyo-game-show-2026-cancelled-on-last-day-due-to-approaching-typhoon-dujuan\n- Tokyo Game Show 2026 official site: https://tgs.cesa.or.jp/2026/en\n",
    "publishedAt": "2026-09-20",
