    "slug": "cyberpunk-edgerunners-2-30-days-out-supporting-cast-sal-bigelow-braindance-paradise-avida-yang-2026",
    "pillar": "anime",
    "title": "Edgerunners 2 Is 30 Days Out. Meet the People Around the Crew.",
    "headline": "Thirty Days.\nNight City's\nSupporting Cast.",
    "subhead": "CD Projekt's Japanese account has been dropping one character a week. The latest three tell you what kind of story this is: a braindance dealer from the comics, his engineer, and the jazz singer who used to love the crew's washed-up legend.",
    "description": "Cyberpunk: Edgerunners 2 hits Netflix Oct. 20, 2026. A rundown of the supporting cast CDPR has revealed since late August: Sal Bigelow (from the Big City Dreams comic), Jessie, and Avida Yang, plus the four leads and what the reveals say about the plot.",
    "keywords": [
      "Cyberpunk Edgerunners 2 cast",
      "Edgerunners 2 Sal Bigelow",
      "Edgerunners 2 Avida Yang",
      "Edgerunners 2 characters",
      "Cyberpunk Edgerunners 2 October 20",
      "Edgerunners 2 Weak Kingsley",
      "Edgerunners 2 Talia Yang",
      "Big City Dreams comic anime",
      "Edgerunners 2 countdown",
      "Sneakz and Beatz",
      "PHRHX",
      "Black-owned media"
    ],
    "ogHeadline": "EDGERUNNERS 2.\n30 DAYS.",
    "ogAccent": "F5D000",
    "heroImage": "https://img.youtube.com/vi/E3Zk2270um8/maxresdefault.jpg",
    "heroCredit": "Netflix / CD PROJEKT RED / Studio Trigger, via Netflix Tudum",
    "heroCreditUrl": "https://www.cyberpunk.net/en/edgerunners2",
    "trendScore": 77,
    "body": "One month. Oct. 20, Netflix, ten episodes. We've covered the leads, the dub, the Cure opening, the Overwatch skins and the board game. What we haven't covered is the bench, and CD Projekt has been quietly filling it in every week.\n\n## The weekly drops\nSince late August, [@CDPRJP](https://x.com/CDPRJP) has been posting one character introduction at a time, and the English side of the fandom mostly missed them. Three matter.\n\n**Avida Yang** (Akemi Okamura). Talia's mother. Weak Kingsley's former lover. A onetime jazz singer and corporate insider. That's three of the four leads tied to one woman: the Maelstrom girl, the washed-up legend, and whatever corp history sent Talia into the gangs in the first place. Okamura is Nami in *One Piece*; that's the weight the role's being given.\n\n**Sal Bigelow** (Takashi Matsuyama). Runs Sal Bigelow's Braindance Paradise. He didn't start in the anime; he's from *Cyberpunk 2077: Big City Dreams*, the Dark Horse comic. Pulling a comic-only character into a Trigger series is the first time this franchise's tie-ins have talked to each other on screen.\n\n**Jessie** (Miho Okasaki). Braindance engineer at Sal's shop. When a show introduces the person who edits the memories, the memories are going to be evidence.\n\n## What the leads look like now\nRoman Carax, the cinephile who records Night City's ugliest truths. Talia Yang, corp-raised, Maelstrom-chromed. Weak Kingsley, the legend living without chrome, voiced in English by Clancy Brown. D, the nomad netrunner hunting his clan's killer. Season 1 was a kid and a gun. This is a documentarian, a braindance parlor and a memory economy. Writer Bartosz Sztybor pitched it to Trigger as *Pulp Fiction* meets *Léon*; the cast list reads like the first one.\n\n## The runway\nThe Cure's \"10:15 Saturday Night\" opens it. Petite Meller's \"Watson\" closes it. The *Hunted* board game ships around Sept. 30 if you want to lose the old crew on a kitchen table first. And 2077 itself is off Game Pass now, so if the show sends you back to the game, that's a purchase, not a sub.\n\n## The read\nBraindance was the thing 2077 built its best missions around and the thing the first anime barely touched. A dealer, an engineer and a mother with a corporate past say Season 2 is going to run on it. Thirty days.\n\n## Sources\n- Wikipedia (compiled cast list with sourced CDPR JP posts), Cyberpunk: Edgerunners 2: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cyberpunk:_Edgerunners_2\n- CD PROJEKT RED Japan on X, Sept. 10, 2026, Jessie character introduction: https://x.com/CDPRJP/status/2098026803151741096\n- CD PROJEKT RED Japan on X, Sept. 3, 2026, Sal Bigelow character introduction: https://x.com/CDPRJP/status/2095507965310816425\n- CD PROJEKT RED Japan on X, Aug. 27, 2026, Avida Yang character introduction: https://x.com/CDPRJP/status/2092961939903103417\n- Anime News Network, July 1, 2026, Edgerunners 2 Japanese and English casts: https://www.animenewsnetwork.com/news/2026-06-30/cyberpunk-edgerunners-2-anime-reveals-japanese-english-casts/.239137\n- Cyberpunk.net, Edgerunners 2 official page: https://www.cyberpunk.net/en/edgerunners2\n",
    "publishedAt": "2026-09-20",
