    "headline": "Blueface Was Swatted Again.\nThat's Four Since July.",
    "subhead": "Police showed up mid-livestream on September 19 while Nevaeh Akira and their infant son were in the house. Blueface's response: it 'comes with the game.'",
    "description": "Blueface was swatted for the fourth time since July on September 19, 2026, during a livestream with Nevaeh Akira and their son; a timeline of the Canyon.",
    "keywords": [
      "Blueface swatted",
      "Blueface swatting",
      "Nevaeh Akira",
      "Blueface livestream",
      "King of Crabs",
      "Santa Clarita",
      "Canyon Country",
      "Miami swatting",
      "Kick livestream",
      "swatting rappers 2026",
      "Sneakz and Beatz",
      "PHRHX",
      "Black-owned media"
    ],
    "ogHeadline": "BLUEFACE WAS SWATTED AGAIN.\nTHAT'S FOUR SINCE JULY.",
    "ogAccent": "B3001B",
    "heroImage": "https://www.hotnewhiphop.com/imgprst/2292x1200-fit-81-auto/2026/09/Blueface-Swatted-Nevaeh-Their-Son-scaled.jpg",
    "heroCredit": "HotNewHipHop",
    "heroCreditUrl": "https://www.hotnewhiphop.com/1010392-blueface-swatted-nevaeh-their-son",
    "heroFocus": "center top",
    "trendScore": 78,
    "body": "Police came to Blueface's house again on Saturday, September 19, in the middle of a livestream, with Nevaeh Akira and their infant son Johnathan Jr. in the room. [AllHipHop](https://allhiphop.com/news/blueface-gets-swatted-again-as-fourth-police-scare-extends-dangerous-pattern/) counted it Sunday as the fourth swatting since July. Video from the stream shows Akira carrying the baby out to talk to officers and confirm nobody was hurt. Blueface's take, paraphrased by AllHipHop: it \"comes with the game,\" because when you live-stream, \"everything's live,\" and some viewers want to feel they have an effect on the broadcast.\n\nHe is not wrong about the mechanism. He is wrong that it is a cost of doing business.\n\n## The timeline\n\nAllHipHop lays out all four. July 21, Canyon Country: a caller claimed multiple people were dead inside and that Blueface had killed his girlfriend and was restraining a child. Deputies surrounded the house; everyone was fine. August 23, King of Crabs in Santa Clarita: a false report of a shooting victim and an armed man. Blueface was pulled out at gunpoint on a Kick stream, and Akira and their days-old newborn were put in a police vehicle. [Complex covered that one](https://www.complex.com/pop-culture/a/backwoodsaltar/blueface-swatted-king-crabs-santa-clarita) the next morning. September 13, Miami: officers removed Blueface and others at gunpoint after another false emergency call. Then Saturday.\n\n[HotNewHipHop](https://www.hotnewhiphop.com/1010392-blueface-swatted-nevaeh-their-son) notes the stream that got swatted was the usual Blueface content: an on-and-off argument with Akira about whether they are broken up, him claiming he was \"just testing her\" after saying he kicked her out, insults traded with laughter. That is the show. The show is what draws the callers.\n\n## Why the pattern is the story\n\nFour false calls in 60 days across two states is not random. It is either one person with a grudge and a VPN or a group of viewers who have learned that a 911 call is the fastest way to appear on screen. Either way, AllHipHop reports that authorities have not identified a suspect or confirmed whether the incidents are linked. Nobody has been charged.\n\nThat is the part that should bother you. Swatting has killed people; the 2017 Wichita case put a caller in federal prison for 20 years. Every one of these responses involves officers arriving expecting a homicide at a Black man's house. The math on that goes bad eventually, and it goes bad for the people inside, not the caller.\n\n## The streaming economy runs on this\n\nBlueface's income right now is the stream. Kick and the rest pay for hours and reactions, and the chaos is the product. A swatting is, in the coldest possible terms, engagement. That is why his answer is a shrug: the same content that gets him swatted is the content that pays the rent, and the platforms that take their cut have no incentive to stop it.\n\nCompare that to the labels of 20 years ago, which at least had a security budget. The creator economy handed Black entertainers the camera and kept the liability with them.\n\n## The take\n\nThere is a newborn in this story. Four times since July a child has been carried out to meet officers with guns drawn because strangers wanted a reaction from a livestream. Blueface can call it the game. It is not; it is a man being targeted, a platform profiting, and a police department that keeps rolling out heavy each time because it cannot afford not to. Somebody in Los Angeles County or Miami-Dade should be tracing calls instead of clearing scenes.\n\n## Sources\n- [Blueface Gets Swatted Again As Fourth Police Scare Extends Dangerous Pattern](https://allhiphop.com/news/blueface-gets-swatted-again-as-fourth-police-scare-extends-dangerous-pattern/) — AllHipHop, September 20, 2026\n- [Blueface Gets Swatted Again, This Time With Nevaeh & Their Son](https://www.hotnewhiphop.com/1010392-blueface-swatted-nevaeh-their-son) — HotNewHipHop, September 20, 2026\n- [Blueface Detained at Gunpoint Mid-Stream in Apparent Swatting at His Restaurant](https://www.complex.com/pop-culture/a/backwoodsaltar/blueface-swatted-king-crabs-santa-clarita) — Complex, August 24, 2026\n",
