    "heroCredit": "GamesRadar",
    "heroCreditUrl": "https://www.gamesradar.com/games/action-rpg/we-dont-have-an-excuse-control-resonant-day-1-patch-fixes-major-issues-but-causes-a-bigger-headache-for-pc-players-who-now-have-to-reinstall-the-whole-92-gb-game/",
    "heroFocus": "center",
    "trendScore": 86,
    "body": "Reviews said the fights were too hard. Remedy heard it, and fixed it an hour before the doors opened.\n\n## What the patch changed\nThe launch hotfix lowers base health and stun thresholds for most enemies, the Dancer and Deserter bosses included. It raises the cap on Aberrant and Ability Strength, puts more Reset Items in vendors, cuts respec costs, and makes The Artist boss drop two Reset Items. That's a studio turning down the heat and making it cheaper to rebuild your character when you guess wrong. ([Push Square](https://www.pushsquare.com/news/2026/09/control-resonant-made-easier-after-player-feedback-ps5-patch-live-now))\n\n## The 92GB problem\nOn PS5 it installed quietly. On Steam, anyone who pre-loaded had to download the whole 92GB game again. Remedy owned it straight up: \"This was an oversight on our part. We don't have an excuse.\" No spin, no \"we're investigating.\" That matters, because day-one goodwill is thin and it burns fast. ([GamesRadar](https://www.gamesradar.com/games/action-rpg/we-dont-have-an-excuse-control-resonant-day-1-patch-fixes-major-issues-but-causes-a-bigger-headache-for-pc-players-who-now-have-to-reinstall-the-whole-92-gb-game/))\n\n## The reviewers noticed\nPC Gamer's reviewer wrote that the hotfix fixes his main complaint from the review. Push Square gave it an 8 out of 10. The 84 on Metacritic came in before the patch, so some of the harshest knocks were aimed at a version that no longer exists. ([PC Gamer](https://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/control-resonant-embarrasses-me-specifically-with-a-launch-day-hotfix-negating-my-main-review-complaint/))\n\n## Why it matters for the lane\nThis is the single-player story game you've got before *GTA 6* eats November. Remedy switched Control from a shooter to a melee action RPG, played as Dylan Faden in a warped Manhattan. The question was never the world. It was the combat. One patch in, the studio's answer is: we'll meet you halfway.\n\nListen to the room, move fast, take the L in public when you earn it. That's how a small studio keeps a loyal crowd. It works for labels too.\n\nBuilt for the culture. Operated by PHRHX through Sneakz & Beatz LLC. Black-owned, four pillars: sneakers, hip-hop, anime, gaming.\n\n## Sources\n- [GamesRadar, Sept. 24, 2026](https://www.gamesradar.com/games/action-rpg/we-dont-have-an-excuse-control-resonant-day-1-patch-fixes-major-issues-but-causes-a-bigger-headache-for-pc-players-who-now-have-to-reinstall-the-whole-92-gb-game/)\n- [Push Square, Sept. 2026](https://www.pushsquare.com/news/2026/09/control-resonant-made-easier-after-player-feedback-ps5-patch-live-now)\n- [PC Gamer, Sept. 2026](https://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/control-resonant-embarrasses-me-specifically-with-a-launch-day-hotfix-negating-my-main-review-complaint/)\n",
