    "heroCreditUrl": "https://www.hotnewhiphop.com/1008061-hip-hop-albums-september-2026",
    "heroFocus": "center",
    "trendScore": 80,
    "body": "Friday gives you two lanes. Pick one, or run both back to back.\n\n## Tee Grizzley, They Forgot\nDetroit's Tee Grizzley drops *They Forgot* on 300 Entertainment: 16 tracks. The singles set it up: \"Back Ina Yams,\" \"No Effort 2,\" and \"Rain\" with Skilla Baby and Ashanti. The title reads like a callout, and the context backs it up. A Michigan judge recently granted him a full expungement of his criminal record. That's a clean slate on paper to go with a comeback on wax. ([BroadwayWorld](https://www.broadwayworld.com/bwwmusic/article/Tee-Grizzley-Announces-New-Album-THEY-FORGOT-Shares-BACK-INA-YAMS-Video-20260821), [HNHH](https://www.hotnewhiphop.com/1008061-hip-hop-albums-september-2026))\n\n## Why Grizzley still matters\n\"First Day Out\" was 2016. It opened a door for the whole Detroit wave that came after. Ten years later, the Ashanti feature tells you who he's aiming at: people who grew up on her and on him, the 25-to-45 crowd that actually buys albums.\n\n## Apollo Brown and Skyzoo, Luxury Tax\nOn the other side, Apollo Brown and Skyzoo reunite for *Luxury Tax*, a decade after *The Easy Truth*. Apollo produced all of it. Singles: \"No Discounts\" and \"God Given.\" This is sample-based, lyric-first rap from a Detroit producer and a Brooklyn writer who never chased a playlist. ([HNHH](https://www.hotnewhiphop.com/1008061-hip-hop-albums-september-2026))\n\n## The bigger picture\nOne is a label album with radio features. The other is a producer-and-rapper record built the old way. Both come out of Detroit's sound in different ways, and both are Black artists making full-length albums in a singles economy. That's the part of hip-hop the timeline skips.\n\nStream both. Buy the vinyl if they press it. Albums only stay viable if people treat them like albums.\n\nBuilt for the culture. Operated by PHRHX through Sneakz & Beatz LLC. Black-owned, four pillars: sneakers, hip-hop, anime, gaming.\n\n## Sources\n- [HNHH, Sept. 2026](https://www.hotnewhiphop.com/1008061-hip-hop-albums-september-2026)\n- [BroadwayWorld, Aug. 21, 2026](https://www.broadwayworld.com/bwwmusic/article/Tee-Grizzley-Announces-New-Album-THEY-FORGOT-Shares-BACK-INA-YAMS-Video-20260821)\n- [Wikipedia: 2026 in hip-hop](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2026_in_hip-hop)\n",
