    "heroFocus": "center",
    "trendScore": 84,
    "body": "If you had an alarm set for Friday, cancel it. J Balvin's Air Jordan 4 moved.\n\n## The new dates\nSneaker Bar Detroit reports the pair, IW2872-700 in Lemonade/Lemonade at $225 in men's sizing, now releases Monday, September 28 on jbalvin.com, then goes global October 2. Balvin opened email sign-ups on his site Thursday. Calendars had it for September 25. Nike hasn't posted its own launch page yet, so treat the dates as reported. ([Sneaker Bar Detroit](https://sneakerbardetroit.com/j-balvin-air-jordan-4-amazonas/))\n\n## The new name\nIt was nicknamed \"Lemonade.\" It's now \"Amazonas,\" after the yellow crocodiles of the Colombian Amazon. The upper is yellow croc-textured leather. The lace tags say \"Just Do It\" on one side and \"Solo Hazlo\" on the other, and the heels carry J Balvin and Jumpman branding. An earlier report tied the colors to Medellín sunsets and Caño Cristales, the river people call the \"river of five colors.\" ([Sneaker Bar Detroit](https://sneakerbardetroit.com/j-balvin-air-jordan-4-lemonade-iw2872-700/))\n\n## Where it fits\nIt's his fourth Jordan silhouette, after the 1, the 2 and the 3. He wore it at the 2026 World Cup opening ceremony, which is about as big a stage as a shoe gets before retail.\n\n## Should you care\nA loud one-color 4 isn't for everybody. But Jordan Brand putting a Colombian artist's culture on its most-wanted silhouette is how the Jumpman stays global. Balvin opened with his own site first, the same way J. Cole did his Fayetteville launch this week. Artists who own the first sale own the relationship. That's the lesson, whether you rock yellow croc or not.\n\nBuilt for the culture. Operated by PHRHX through Sneakz & Beatz LLC. Black-owned, four pillars: sneakers, hip-hop, anime, gaming.\n\n## Sources\n- [Sneaker Bar Detroit, Sept. 24, 2026](https://sneakerbardetroit.com/j-balvin-air-jordan-4-amazonas/)\n- [Sneaker Bar Detroit, 2026](https://sneakerbardetroit.com/j-balvin-air-jordan-4-lemonade-iw2872-700/)\n"