    "heroImage": "https://www.hotnewhiphop.com/imgprst/2292x1200-fit-81-auto/2026/09/Screenshot-2026-09-24-at-08.14.29-e1790252146746.png",
    "body": "**Status: unreleased sample. No style code, no price, no date.** Anything past that is speculation, and we label it that way.\n\n## What surfaced\nOn September 24, [HotNewHipHop](https://www.hotnewhiphop.com/1010744-hiroshi-fujiwara-unreleased-fragment-x-travis-scott-x-air-jordan-1-low-sneaker-news) ran photos of Hiroshi Fujiwara wearing a Travis Scott x Fragment Air Jordan 1 Low nobody can buy: black upper, bright blue toe box and heel, a white reversed Swoosh over the \"Cactus Jack/Fragment\" text, cream midsole and blue outsole. He wore them with an all-black fit like they were beaters.\n\n## It matches the June tease\nIn June, Fujiwara posted a grayscale image to his Instagram story and deleted it quickly. [House of Heat](https://houseofheat.co/jordan/travis-scott-fragment-air-jordan-1-low-2026) and [Sneaker Bar Detroit](https://sneakerbardetroit.com/hiroshi-fujiwara-fragment-travis-scott-air-jordan-1-low/) worked out the colors from it: blue toe and heel, black panels, white reverse Swoosh, sail midsole. This week's pair matches. So it's not a new colorway. It's the June design on his feet in real life, which is a bigger step than a deleted story.\n\n![June 2026 Fragment x Travis Scott AJ1 Low tease](https://sneakerbardetroit.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/hiroshi-fujiwara-fragment-travis-scott-air-jordan-1-low-2026.webp \"Sneaker Bar Detroit|https://sneakerbardetroit.com/hiroshi-fujiwara-fragment-travis-scott-air-jordan-1-low/\")\n\n## Why nobody's calling it a release yet\nHiroshi wears samples all the time. The original three-way collab spent three years as a tease, from his feet at a 2022 event to the actual 2025 release. SBD notes it's still unknown whether this pair is a sample, a friends-and-family pair, or headed for retail. (HNHH's piece calls the original low a 2021 shoe. It released in 2025.)\n\n## The numbers behind the hype\nThe 2025 Travis x Fragment AJ1 Low drew more than **4.4 million unique raffle entries**, per SBD, the most ever recorded for a sneaker. That's why a sighting on one man's feet is sneaker news. Nike knows the demand is there before it prints a single box.\n\n## The read\nThe Travis-and-Hiroshi AJ1 run works because two people outside the Swoosh control the design, and Nike collects most of the profit when resellers flip them at five times retail. If this pair is real, the question is the same as always: whether regular people get a real chance at retail or it's another raffle where bots win.\n\nRelated: [Travis Scott AJ1 Low 'Red Chicago' reportedly set for 2027](https://sneakzandbeatz.com/the-lane/travis-scott-air-jordan-1-low-red-chicago-2027-report).\n\n## Sources\n- HotNewHipHop, Sept. 24, 2026: [Hiroshi Fujiwara wears unreleased Fragment x Travis Scott x Air Jordan 1 Low](https://www.hotnewhiphop.com/1010744-hiroshi-fujiwara-unreleased-fragment-x-travis-scott-x-air-jordan-1-low-sneaker-news)\n- House of Heat, June 2026: [Travis Scott x Fragment Air Jordan 1 Low 2026 tease](https://houseofheat.co/jordan/travis-scott-fragment-air-jordan-1-low-2026)\n- Sneaker Bar Detroit, June 2026: [Did Hiroshi Fujiwara just tease another Travis Scott Fragment Jordan 1 Low?](https://sneakerbardetroit.com/hiroshi-fujiwara-fragment-travis-scott-air-jordan-1-low/)\n",
